# SPEC-011 — Project Wizard
Version: 1.0
Status: Approved
Phase: Sprint 1
Category: Feature Specification

---

# Purpose

The Project Wizard is the creator's first conversation with Sonic AI V3.

It is not simply a form.

It is the intentional beginning of a creative journey.

Every decision made here becomes part of the project's identity and history.

The wizard should feel calm, intelligent, and inspiring—not bureaucratic.

---

# User Promise

"Creating a new project should feel like stepping into a professional studio with an experienced collaborator already prepared to help."

---

# Primary Question

"What are we creating?"

---

# Objectives

• Remove friction from starting.
• Capture only essential information.
• Establish project identity.
• Generate meaningful metadata.
• Prepare the workspace.
• Preserve creative momentum.

---

# Wizard Flow

Step 1
Project Identity

• Project Name
• Artist
• Optional Cover Image

---

Step 2
Creative Direction

• Genre
• BPM
• Musical Key
• Mood
• Reference Artists
• Reference Tracks

---

Step 3
Production Intent

What are we making?

Examples

• Single
• EP
• Album
• Beat
• Demo
• Mix
• Master
• Sound Design
• Film Score

---

Step 4
Notes

Free-form ideas

Lyrics

Voice memos

Concepts

Goals

Inspirations

---

Step 5
Review

Display everything clearly.

Allow editing.

One final action:

Create Project

---

# Defaults

Status = Draft

Creative State = Exploring

Intent = Create

Session Count = 0

Completion = 0%

---

# AI Responsibilities

Never overwhelm.

Offer suggestions only when useful.

Example:

"This BPM is common in modern trap."

"This key pairs well with..."

"Would you like to import a reference track?"

Always optional.

Never intrusive.

---

# Backend Requirements

POST /projects

Generate Project ID

Generate timestamps

Initialize project metadata

Create initial timeline event

Create initial session

---

# Success Criteria

✓ Project created successfully

✓ Opens immediately in Project Workspace

✓ Appears instantly on Dashboard

✓ Appears in Recent Projects

✓ Initial session created

✓ Timeline initialized

✓ No data loss

✓ Undo available until first save